> The key to this dish is getting a golden sear on the tofu cubes before braising. Don't crowd the pan—fry in batches if needed. The contrast between the crispy exterior and silky interior is what makes braised tofu special.

== Fry the Tofu ==

Heat @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in a #pan{}. Add the @extra-firm tofu{350%g} (cubed into 2 cm pieces) and fry, turning occasionally, until golden on several sides, about ~{5-6%minutes}. Remove and set aside.

== Sauté Aromatics and Mushrooms ==

Add another drizzle of @neutral oil{½%tbsp} if the pan looks dry. Add:
- @ginger{2%slices}
- @scallions{1%stalk} (sliced)
- @fresh shiitake mushrooms{250%g} (halved)

Sauté for ~{2%minutes} until the mushrooms begin to soften and release their fragrance.

== Braise ==

In a small bowl, mix the sauce:
- @chicken broth{250%ml}
- @oyster sauce{2%tbsp}
- @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}
- @sugar{1%tsp}

Pour the sauce into the pan and return the tofu. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat to a gentle simmer. Cover and cook for ~{15%minutes}, allowing the flavors to meld and the sauce to reduce slightly.

== Thicken ==

In a small cup, mix the slurry: @cornstarch{1%tsp} and @cold water{1%tbsp}.

Push the tofu to the side, stir in the cornstarch slurry, and cook for ~{1%minute} until the sauce becomes glossy and coats the spoon. Stir everything together and serve over rice.